### Case Summary ###
**Clinical Impression (Provisional):**  
- **Primary Psychotic Disorder, unspecified** (e.g., schizophreniform disorder or early-stage schizophrenia), given:  
  • Duration ~7 months (meets >1-month threshold for schizophreniform; <6 months would be required for that diagnosis — *but 7 months exceeds it*, so schizophrenia is possible if functional decline persists);  
  • Presence of **one first-rank delusion** (thought insertion/withdrawal — “aliens stealing my thoughts”);  
  • Prominent **negative symptoms**: avolition, asociality, blunted affect, anhedonia;  
  • No confirmed hallucinations, disorganized speech, or catatonia per self-report;  
  • No evidence of mood episode, substance use, or general medical condition *to date*.  

- **Rule Out Organic Etiologies**, particularly:  
  • **Autoimmune encephalitis** (e.g., anti-NMDA-R, anti-D2R, anti-GABA-B-R);  
  • **Metabolic/toxic encephalopathy** (though initial labs unrevealing);  
  • **Neurodegenerative or paraneoplastic syndromes** (hence FDG-PET, CSF cytology, antibody panels);  
  • **Late-onset schizophrenia-spectrum disorder vs. atypical neurodegeneration** (e.g., early FTD variant) — though less likely without cognitive or motor signs *yet*.  

**Next Steps (Implied):**  
- Await results of MRI brain, EEG, CSF studies, autoimmune serologies, and FDG-PET.  
- Consider formal neuropsychological assessment and structured psychiatric interview (e.g., SCID-5).  
- Initiate shared decision-making regarding antipsychotic trial *if organic causes are ruled out*, with emphasis on low-dose, slow titration and close monitoring for side effects (e.g., EPS, metabolic parameters).  
- Psychosocial support: engagement strategies, supported housing/ACT team referral if functional impairment remains severe.  

No treatment has been initiated or discussed in the dialogue. All test results remain pending.

